first my colleague from Vermont Bernie  Sanders thank you money and I want to  congratulate you for your continued  leadership in this area um I get around  the state of Vermont a whole lot and I  talked to many people all over the  country and what people are saying to me  is that in this country the richest  country in the history of the world  there is something very wrong that 43  million Americans have no health  insurance at all and millions more are  under insured and as Barney Frank just  indicated it makes no sense at all to be  talking about putting another hundred  and ten billion into the military as the  president would like or even worse a  hundred and forty plus into the defense  as the Republicans want when millions of  people have no health insurance millions  of more have inadequate health insurance  and tens of millions are unable to  afford the prescription drugs that they  desperately need it it makes no sense to  me to be spending a hundred billion  dollars a year defending Europe and Asia  against non-existent enemies when in  this country we have by far the highest  rate of childhood poverty in the  industrialized world when we have over  twenty percent of our kids living in  poverty when senior citizens all over  this country cannot afford basic needs  by keeping their homes warm or paying  for their out-of-pocket health care that  they need the two basic issues are  number one given the end of the Cold War  given the collapse of the Soviet Union  does any sensible person really believe  that we need to spend billions and  billions  more on the military there's any  sensible person believe that our  military posture should be to  simultaneously be fighting two wars  without any allies to protect us despite  all of the money that NATO spends and I  think the obvious answer is no there is  enormous waste in the military right now  we all know that we all know that pork  is rampant where various districts get  money for the military that is not  needed so the truth of the matter is we  can have the strongest defense in the  world we can raise the pay and the  benefits that our military does need but  you don't have to spend more money on  the defense or the CIA or the  intelligence budget to do that but the  most important point that I want to make  is that we have got to get our  priorities straight we cannot continue  to cut back on Medicare we cannot  continue to have Medicaid paying in my  state about one-third of the normal  reimbursements that physicians and  hospitals get we cannot continue to have  millions of people spending fifty sixty  percent of their limited incomes on  housing at the same time as we cut back  on affordable housing in this great  country what we have got to do is make  sure that all of our people have a  decent standard of living not continuing  to cut cut and cut on the needs of  working families senior citizens  veterans low-income people and then say  to the military hey we can give you  everything you need and and then some  more so I think for those of us who  believe in insane priorities in this  country but those of us who believe that  every American is entitled to a decent  standard of living we have got to stand  up and oppose this outrageous proposal  to increase military spending thank you  very much
 

